  "description": "<div>\n  <p>Each entry in <code>tasks</code> is a one-unit job labelled by a capital letter. A processor handles one job per time unit or remains idle. Between two jobs with the same letter, at least <code>n</code> complete time units must be occupied by other jobs or idle slots. Return the shortest total elapsed time to finish all jobs.</p>\n  <p>You may reorder jobs freely. If there are no tasks, the elapsed time is zero.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> tasks = [\"A\",\"A\",\"A\",\"B\",\"B\",\"B\"], n = 2\n<strong>Output:</strong> 8</pre>\n  <p>A B idle A B idle A B takes eight slots.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> tasks = [\"A\",\"C\",\"A\"], n = 1\n<strong>Output:</strong> 3</pre>\n  <p>A C A meets the one-slot separation without idling.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> tasks = [\"A\",\"A\",\"A\"], n = 3\n<strong>Output:</strong> 9</pre>\n  <p>A idle idle idle A idle idle idle A takes nine slots.</p>\n  <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><code>0 &lt;= tasks.length &lt;= 100</code>; each entry is a one-character uppercase English letter.</li>\n    <li><code>0 &lt;= n &lt;= 100</code>.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>",
